---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-07-vet-view.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-07',
  title: 'New workflow page: Vet View',
  tags: ['workflows', 'vet-view', 'health', 'seo'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 7, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a Vet View workflow page at
    <a href="/workflows/vet-view" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/vet-view</a>
    and corrected every place that said BreederHQ emails health reports to a vet. Email sharing is
    retired: a vet gets a PDF the breeder sends, or a PIN-protected link the breeder can revoke.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">New file</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><code>src/pages/workflows/vet-view.astro</code>: what a Vet View is, the adult animal, offspring, and litter cases, how a link protects the breeder's data (PIN shown once, 72-hour expiry, revoke, session limits, notes opt-in), Download PDF, the mobile app, the stall card, and permissions. Includes FAQPage and HowTo structured data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/workflows" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows</a>: added a Vet View card and narrowed the Medication Tracking card.</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows/medication-tracking" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/medication-tracking</a>: the shareable health records FAQ, how-to step, and section now describe Vet View and link to the new page. The email option is removed.</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows/scout-ai" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/scout-ai</a>, <a href="/" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">homepage</a>, <a href="/for-breeders" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/for-breeders</a>: Scout points to Vet View rather than creating a PIN link itself.</li>
      <li>Species pages for dogs, cats, horses, goats, sheep, and rabbits: the email-to-vet line is replaced with Vet View and Share With Vet.</li>
      <li>Structured data feature list, plan feature list, <code>llms.txt</code>, and the OKF product bundle now describe Vet View.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">SEO</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The new page is picked up by the generated sitemap on the next build. No screenshots yet; they follow separately.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
